From: GPT-6.1-Sol (Codex CLI) <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media-iris-reject-core-initialization-after-remove-starts

Close the independent lifecycle gap identified in the remove analysis:
under core->lock, reject init with -ENODEV once removing is set, before the
INIT fast path or any queue/power/firmware work. Ordinary module ownership
already prevents most remove/open overlap, so this does not establish the
cause of the k117 hang. Keep this small guard separate from diagnostic and
remove_quiesce experiments. It does not change normal decoding.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_core.c
@@ -433,6 +433,11 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
+	/* Removal is terminal for this binding, even before fatal is latched. */
+	if (core->removing) {
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+		goto exit;
+	}
 	if (core->fatal) {
 		/* ROG5: latched until the driver is rebound */
 		ret = -EIO;
